# Conventions

> Style, naming, and formatting rules for this project. Language- and framework-specific rules come first; the project-wide rules after them apply to every stack.

{{STACK_CONVENTIONS}}

## Project-wide

### Comments

- One-line comments for "why", not "what".
- No comment blocks longer than 3 lines.
- TODOs name an owner and a ticket: `TODO(<owner>): <description> — <ticket>`.

### Git

- Conventional commits: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`, e.g. `feat(auth): add login endpoint`.
- Types: feat, fix, docs, refactor, test, chore, perf, ci, build.
- Max 72 characters in the subject line.
- Branch naming: `feat/<description>`, `fix/<description>`.
- No commits directly to `main`. Use branches and PRs.

### Tests

- Every test is tagged `<feature>/R<n>` for the requirement it verifies (see `docs/tdd.md`).
- Test names describe behavior, using the naming style of the stack rules above.
- One assertion per test where possible.
- Prefer real temp directories over mocks for filesystem tests, and clean up afterwards (temp dirs, env vars).
